---
import DocLayout from '../../layouts/DocLayout.astro';
const sections: [string, string][] = [
  ['upload', 'Upload a file'], ['download', 'Download a file'], ['continue', 'Pause and continue'], ['directory', 'The shared directory'], ['limits', 'Limits'],
];
---
<DocLayout title="File transfers" description="Upload local files to a paired machine and download files from its shared directory, with pause and continue." lead="Open Files in Mob for the selected machine. Upload with your device's file picker, or download a remote file and choose where to save it." sections={sections}>
  <section id="upload">
    <h2>Upload a file</h2>
    <p>Choose <strong>Upload file</strong> and select a local file. Mob prepares a private copy, shows progress, then verifies the received file before making it available in the remote directory shown on screen. If the name already exists, the new file receives a suffix; the existing file is kept.</p>
    <p>Copy the displayed directory path into your conversation and ask the agent to use the uploaded file. File uploads are separate from chat image attachments.</p>
  </section>
  <section id="download">
    <h2>Download a file</h2>
    <p>Choose <strong>Download</strong> beside a remote file. After the download and integrity check finish, choose <strong>Save</strong> and pick a local destination. Dismissing the save picker keeps the verified download available to save later.</p>
    <p>To retrieve a file from another directory on the remote machine, ask the agent to copy it into the directory displayed in Files, then refresh the list. Ask the agent to create a ZIP archive when you need a folder.</p>
  </section>
  <section id="continue">
    <h2>Pause and continue</h2>
    <p>Use <strong>Pause</strong> to keep the partial transfer. After a network interruption or app restart, choose <strong>Continue</strong> or <strong>Retry</strong>. Mobile transfers pause when Mob goes into the background; return to the app and continue them.</p>
    <p><strong>Cancel</strong> removes the local transfer copy and any unfinished upload on the remote machine. A completed remote file remains available. If a remote file changes during download, cancel that download and start it again so that its contents come from one version.</p>
  </section>
  <section id="directory">
    <h2>The shared directory</h2>
    <p>Files are stored in <code>~/mob-files</code> on the office computer, on macOS and Linux. It is an ordinary folder, so you can also open it there and add or remove files yourself. The app shows its absolute path. The folder belongs to the machine and is shared by its paired devices and agents. Deleting a conversation does not remove these files.</p>
    <p>To use another folder, set <code>filesDir</code> in <code>config.json</code> or <code>MOBD_FILES_DIR</code>, then restart mobd. History, pairings and settings are stored separately and do not move with it.</p>
    <p>Only ordinary files directly inside this folder appear in the list. Subfolders, symbolic links and names starting with a dot are excluded. Unfinished uploads wait in its hidden <code>.uploads</code> folder and appear only once they are complete and verified.</p>
  </section>
  <section id="limits">
    <h2>Limits</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Files needs a mobd that supports it. An older mobd displays an upgrade explanation.</li>
      <li>Uploads are limited to 20 GiB per file. Leave free disk space on both devices for the file and temporary copies.</li>
      <li>Keep Mob open while transferring on iOS and Android. Transfers do not continue in the background.</li>
      <li>Paused uploads remain on the remote machine until canceled. There is no automatic expiry.</li>
      <li>Manage completed remote files through the agent or on the remote machine. Files has no remote delete or folder synchronization action.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</DocLayout>
